  "notes": "NIBOR has no cessation plan. Norges Bank ARR convention: 3M NIBOR below 2Y, 6M NIBOR from 2Y. Front end also trades as 3M IMM FRA strips. NOWA OIS par family is NKS{n}Y / NKS{n}M ('NOK SWAP OIS', live 1M-30Y, found 2026-07 — earlier probe of NKSWTN/NKSO/NKSN/NKOIS missed the short root). Beware NKSF{n}Y which LOOKS right but is CHF-NOK FX FORWARDS. OIS conventions assumed Annual ACT/365F payLag 1 (NOWA is a 365-basis rate) — verify vs SWPM. Discounting stays SELF off NIBOR; NOWA discounting for LCH-cleared would be a pricing change. Front end 2026-08-03: direct 6M IMM FRAs NKF60101-0401 at the BGNL source (the plain/BGN forms carry no px — same qualifier lesson as NDFS/BLC), exactly what Bloomberg's YCSW0313 builds from. Replaced the NKF3-3M-strip + NKBFVC-basis frontFromOis synthesis, which sat -3 to -11bp off S0313 sub-18M (the modeled basis, not the strip, was the error term). History of the old path: NOK FRAs published no API px on plain sources (NKFR0CF etc dead), so the front was OIS-shaped (fwd NIBOR = NOWA fwd + NIBOR3M-OIS spread + NKBFVC 3s6s, identity check 2026-07: 13.8 vs 12.2bp), later upgraded to the real NKF3 strip + basis. If BGNL dies, that frontFromOis block is in git history pre-6.2.6. NKSW1 (1Y) DISABLED same day: its 5.05 print implies a Feb-Aug27 forward ~12bp above what the NKF6 strip trades (2x5.053-4.85=5.26 vs FRAs 5.01), and Bloomberg's YCSW0313 omits NKSW1 for the same reason — in Scandinavia the strip IS the front-end market. Re-enable only if its contributors re-align with the strip."
